    77	| [docs/research/](docs/research/) | Literature reviews that shaped the plan |
    78	
    79	## Repository layout
    80	
    81	| Path | What it holds |
    82	|---|---|
    83	| [`analysis/`](analysis/) | Scripts that compute every reported number from `results/` |
    84	| [`train/`](train/) | Training code: SFT, GRPO, prompt/action format |
    85	| [`data/`](data/) | Dataset builders and fixed split files |
    86	| [`eval/`](eval/) | Benchmark harnesses: AndroidControl, AndroidWorld, MobileWorld, general knowledge |
    87	| [`scripts/`](scripts/) | Run orchestration, by purpose (AndroidWorld, MobileWorld, training, speed, publishing) |
    88	| [`results/`](results/) | Raw results (episode files, predictions) and the summaries computed from them |
    89	| [`logs/`](logs/) | Run logs kept as evidence (model servers, emulators, runs, Codex sessions) |
    90	| [`docs/`](docs/) | Documentation |
    91	
    92	## Rules this project kept
    93	
    94	- **No AndroidWorld data in training:** no AndroidWorld tasks, variants, trajectories or checkers in any training set.
    95	- **Fair harness:** same screenshot budget, step budget, quantisation and app list for the compared models.
    96	- **Sealed held-out seeds:** results of seeds 7/1234/2026 were not read until every model had finished that seed.
    97	- **Every deviation is dated** in [docs/PREREG_v4.md](docs/PREREG_v4.md), with what had and had not been seen at the time.
    98	- **Exceptions count as failures**, unlike AndroidWorld's default.
     1	# Results
     2	
     3	Every number below is read from a file in [`results/`](../results/); each section names its source.
     4	To recompute them all, see [reproduce.md](reproduce.md).
     5	
     6	**Contents:** [AndroidWorld held-out](#androidworld-held-out-seeds-primary) ·
     7	[AndroidWorld development seed](#androidworld-development-seed-30) · [MobileWorld](#mobileworld) ·
     8	[Speed](#speed) · [Offline evaluations](#offline-evaluations)
     9	
    10	---
    11	
    12	## AndroidWorld, held-out seeds (primary)
    13	
    14	Preregistered comparison ([PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md)): 116 tasks × seeds 7, 1234, 2026; one run per model per seed.
    15	Source: [`results/sealed_analysis_final.md`](../results/sealed_analysis_final.md) (+ `.json`).
    16	
    17	### Scores
    18	
    19	| Model | Seed 7 | Seed 1234 | Seed 2026 | Total / 348 | Answer tasks / 75 | Action tasks / 273 |
    20	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    21	| **LFM3-VL-2B v4** | 18 | 17 | 19 | **54 (15.5%)** | 13 | 41 |
    22	| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (matched) | 16 | 13 | 18 | 47 (13.5%) | 19 | 28 |
    23	| LFM3-VL-2B v1 | 11 | 10 | 11 | 32 (9.2%) | 0 | 32 |
    24	
    25	- Success = AndroidWorld's checker says the task is done **and** the agent ended the episode.
    26	- Exceptions count as failures.
    27	- "Answer tasks" (25 per seed) need a typed answer; v1 never learned to answer.
    28	
    29	### Comparisons (paired, template-clustered sign-flip test, 10,000 draws)
    30	
    31	| Comparison | Difference | 95% CI | p | Verdict |
    32	|---|---|---|---|---|
    33	| **v4 − GUI-Owl (primary)** | **+2.0 pts** | [−4.5, +8.6] | 0.60 | **Non-inferior** (lower bound > −6.9); not superior |
    34	| v4 − v1 | +6.3 pts | [+1.1, +11.5] | 0.02 | v4 better |
    35	| v1 − GUI-Owl | −4.3 pts | [−10.6, +1.9] | 0.21 | No significant difference |
    36	
    37	Per-seed exact McNemar tests for v4 − GUI-Owl: p = 0.85, 0.52 and 1.0. No single seed is significant.
    38	
    39	### Sensitivity analyses
    40	
    41	Source: [`results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md`](../results/sealed_sensitivity_final.md). None of these was preregistered.
    42	
    43	| Variant | v4 | GUI-Owl | Difference | 95% CI | Non-inferior? |
    44	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    45	| A. Primary | 54 | 47 | +2.0 | [−4.5, +8.6] | yes |
    46	| B. Drop the 7 pairs that still end in an exception | 54 | 44 | +2.9 | [−3.4, +9.3] | yes |
    47	| B3. Drop 3 templates with scoring-phase exceptions (all seeds) | 54 | 43 | +3.2 | [−3.1, +9.6] | yes |
    48	| **C. Count v4 seed 1234's 113 re-runs as failures** | 37 | 47 | **−2.9** | [−8.4, +2.7] | **no** |
    49	| D. Exclude seed 1234 | 37 | 34 | +1.3 | [−5.8, +8.4] | yes |
    50	| Disputed checker successes counted as failures | 53 | 47 | +1.7 | [−4.8, +8.3] | yes |
    51	
    52	**Key point:** only variant C fails. In C, the preregistered "re-run once if the emulator crashed before step 1"
    53	rule is not applied to v4's seed-1234 episodes. Emulator 2 hung from 00:35 to 08:06 on 2026-11-19, and every v4
    54	seed-1234 episode in that window crashed during task setup.
    55	
    56	### Re-runs and exceptions
    57	
    58	| Arm | Episodes re-run once (setup crash before step 1) | Still an exception after re-run |
    59	|---|---|---|
    60	| v4 | seed 7: 4 · seed 1234: 113 | seed 1234: 4 (counted as failures) |
    61	| GUI-Owl | seed 7: 1 · seed 1234: 1 · seed 2026: 2 | none |
    62	| v1 | seed 2026: 1 | none |
    63	
    64	Not re-run, counted as failures (the crash was not before step 1): v4 seed 1234 BrowserDraw,
    65	v4 seed 2026 SimpleSmsReplyMostRecent, GUI-Owl seed 1234 SimpleSmsSendReceivedAddress.
    66	
    67	### Disputed checker successes
    68	
    69	Every checker success was compared with its saved screenshots. Two contradict the screens. They stay successes in
    70	the primary score and count as failures only in the sensitivity row above.
    71	
    72	| Arm | Seed | Task | Why disputed |
    73	|---|---|---|---|
    74	| v4 | 7 | ClockStopWatchPausedVerify | Stopwatch left running |
    75	| v1 | 2026 | OpenAppTaskEval | Opened Contacts, then deleted the only contact before finishing |
    76	
    77	Source: [`results/aw_checker_disputes.json`](../results/aw_checker_disputes.json).
    78	
    79	### Known limits
    80	
    81	- **Device state is not fully reset between episodes (all models).** AndroidWorld's app-snapshot restore is
    82	  skipped ("Snapshot not found"), so data a task's own setup does not clear can carry over. Bias direction is unknown.
    83	- **Power is limited.** Cluster standard error is about 3.25 points. Detecting superiority with 80% power would need
    84	  about a 9-point true gap.
    85	- **A harness defect affects all models:** gRPC warnings on adb's error output can corrupt adb replies during task
    86	  setup. Those crashes fall under the re-run rule.
    87	- **The interval is nominal.** The 95% CI comes from inverting the sign-flip test, so it assumes symmetric paired
    88	  differences and exact coverage is not guaranteed.
    89	- **GUI-Owl runs in our harness, not its own.** It gets one screenshot at ≤ 1,048,576 pixels and 4-bit weights,
    90	  not its published configuration of 5 screenshots and full resolution. Its published AndroidWorld score is 67.9%.
    91	
    92	---
    93	
    94	## AndroidWorld, development seed 30
    95	
    96	Seed 30 was used to choose between versions, so these are development numbers. Source:
    97	[`results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md`](../results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md).
    98	
    99	| Model | Successes / 116 | Answer / 25 | Action / 91 | Exceptions | Apple M5 s/step (median) |
   100	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   101	| **LFM3-VL-2B v4 (final)** | **18** | 6 | 12 | 4 | 2.96 |
   102	| MAI-UI-2B (1 screenshot, 8-bit) | 32 | 5 | 27 | 1 | 9.35 |
   103	| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (1 screenshot) | 23 | 10 | 13 | 0 | 7.00 |
   104	| Qwen3.5-2B v1 | 16 | 0 | 16 | 2 | 4.20 |
   105	| LFM3-VL-2B v1 | 15 | 0 | 15 | 2 | 2.66 |
   106	| LFM3-VL-2B v3 | 13 | 0 | 13 | 3 | 2.61 |
   107	| Qwen3.5-0.8B v1 | 12 | 0 | 12 | 1 | 2.00 |
   108	| LFM3-VL-2B v1 + runtime feedback (ablation) | 10 | 0 | 10 | 7 | 2.85 |
   109	| LFM3-VL-2B v2 + forced intent (ablation) | 6 | 0 | 6 | 4 | 2.68 |
   110	| LFM3-VL-2B v2 | 3 | 0 | 3 | 5 | 2.61 |
   111	| LFM2.5-VL-450M v1 | 2 | 0 | 2 | 4 | 1.14 |
   112	| LFM3-VL-2B base | 1 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2.13 |
   113	| LFM2.5-VL-450M base | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3 | 2.21 |
   114	
   115	- **MAI-UI-2B is the strongest model on this seed.** It ran later as an extra arm and is not part of the
   116	  preregistered comparison. It needs 8-bit weights because its 4-bit output degenerates
   117	  ([`results/maiui_quant_check.md`](../results/maiui_quant_check.md)). Its official prompt lists AndroidWorld's apps.
   118	- GUI-Owl's seed-30 run did not get the installed-app list that v4 gets. The held-out runs give it to both.
   119	- v4 passed its preregistered development gate on this seed ([`results/v4_gate_seed30.txt`](../results/v4_gate_seed30.txt)).
   120	
   121	---
   122	
   123	## MobileWorld
   124	
   125	Secondary and descriptive: 105 English GUI-only tasks, one run per model, temperature 0, 50 rounds per task.
   126	This compares agent pipelines, not model weights alone. Source:
   127	[`results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md`](../results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md) (+ `.json`).
   128	
   129	### Scores
   130	
   131	| Model | Successes / 105 | Tasks with a result | No result (counted as failure) |
   132	|---|---|---|---|
   133	| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (official agent) | **22 (21.0%)** | 102 | 3 |
   134	| MAI-UI-2B (official agent, 8-bit) | 11 (10.5%) | 98 | 7 |
   135	| LFM3-VL-2B v4 | 6 (5.7%) | 104 | 1 |
   136	
   137	### Paired comparisons (exact McNemar)
   138	
   139	| Comparison | Both solved | Only first | Only second | Difference | p |
   140	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   141	| v4 vs GUI-Owl | 6 | 0 | 16 | −15.2 pts | 3.05 × 10⁻⁵ |
   142	| MAI-UI vs v4 | 4 | 7 | 2 | +4.8 pts | 0.18 |
   143	| MAI-UI vs GUI-Owl | 9 | 2 | 13 | −10.5 pts | 0.0074 |
   144	
   145	### Sensitivity (environment problems)
   146	
   147	| Tasks kept | v4 | GUI-Owl | MAI-UI |
   148	|---|---|---|---|
   149	| All 105 | 6 | 22 | 11 |
   150	| 97: drop tasks with a setup/scoring failure in the v4 or GUI-Owl run | 6 | 22 | — |
   151	| 87: also drop tasks where v4's or GUI-Owl's device was re-initialised | 5 | 21 | — |
   152	| 89: drop the 16 tasks with an environment problem in MAI-UI's run | 6 | 21 | 11 |
   153	
   154	- **What-if, not a bound:** if MAI-UI had solved the 5 tasks it lost to final setup failures, it would score 16
   155	  vs GUI-Owl's 22 (p = 0.26). GUI-Owl and v4 solved none of those 5.
   156	- MAI-UI ran last, on recreated containers after two spot-VM preemptions. Its emulators crashed with a fatal KVM
   157	  error 17 times. The GUI-Owl and v4 container logs no longer exist, so whether they saw the same crashes is unknown.
   158	
   159	### Settings per model
   160	
   161	| Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl | MAI-UI |
   162	|---|---|---|---|
   163	| Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 (official default) | 1 (official default 3) |
   164	| Text history | last 8 intent/action pairs | all earlier step summaries | official |
   165	| Image budget | ≤ 880×880 px area, ≤ 1,024 tokens | full screen, ≤ 2,600 tokens | full screen, ≤ 2,600 tokens |
   166	| Weights | 4-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit |
   167	| Parse attempts | 2 | 5 | official |
   168	
   169	### Harness notes (disclosed, not corrected)
   170	
   171	- **No user simulator:** `ask_user` needs an LLM-backed simulator this setup lacks. GUI-Owl hit it in 7 executions
   172	  and MAI-UI in 14. v4 has no such action.
   173	- **Typing and Enter cost v4 rounds:** its adapter sends Enter as an extra round after typing. In 3 tasks the
   174	  Enter fell on round 50 and was never sent. 37 tasks that hit the budget had fewer than 50 model decisions.
   175	- **One task fails for every model:** ThanksgivingPrepTask setup failed on every attempt.
   176	- **Discarded runs:** v4's first run (5/105) used an adapter that changed v4's scroll and Enter behaviour, so it is
   177	  not counted. GUI-Owl's first run lost its model server after 4 tasks and was discarded.
   178	
   179	---
   180	
   181	## Speed
   182	
   183	v4 sends far fewer prompt tokens per step (a smaller image) and processes them faster.
   184	
   185	### CPU (Intel Xeon 2.8 GHz, 8 threads, idle GCP n2-standard-16)
   186	
   187	Same 5 screenshots and goals for every model, through each model's own evaluation agent; 4-bit models, llama.cpp
   188	`cd959bae9`. Source: [`results/speed/speed_t8.md`](../results/speed/speed_t8.md).
   189	
   190	| Model | s/step (median) | Prompt tokens | Prompt tokens/s | Output tokens | Server memory |
   191	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   192	| **v4** | **6.4** | 803 | 149 | 28 | 2.8 GB |
   193	| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | 58.0 | 2,570 | 47 | 47 | 7.5 GB* |
   194	| MAI-UI-2B | 58.2 | 2,575 | 48 | 90 | 7.4 GB* |
   195	
   196	\* Inflated by llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache. Model files are 1.30 GB (v4) and 1.55 GB (GUI-Owl, MAI-UI at 4-bit).
   197	
   198	### Apple M5 GPU, measured inside the AndroidWorld seed-30 runs
   199	
   200	Source: [`results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md`](../results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md).
   201	
   202	| Model | Weights | Steps timed | s/step median (p10–p90) | Prompt tokens | Output tokens |
