# MAI-UI-2B: Q4_K_M breaks the output format; Q8_0 does not (2026-11-18)

Found during the first AndroidWorld seed-30 attempt with MAI-UI-2B Q4_K_M (moved to
`results/androidworld/_invalid/maiui_2b_matched_degenerate_1430`): every step's `<thinking>` was empty. Step 1 of each
episode either produced `<thinking>\n<thinking>\n<thinking>\n</thinking><tool_call>...` (33 tokens) or the same pattern
repeated until the 2,048-token cap; the empty replies were then replayed in the history and the agent never planned.

Reproduction on the exact request captured from the agent (`MAIUI_DUMP_DIR`, step 1 of SystemBrightnessMax, official
MAI-UI navigation prompt, screenshot 672x1504, temperature 0, same llama.cpp cd959bae9 Metal server flags as GUI-Owl):

| model file | screenshot 672x1504 | same screenshot at 1088x2400 |
|---|---|---|
| MAI-UI-2B **Q8_0** (1.83 GB) | `<thinking>\nThought: To turn the brightness to the maximum, I should open Settings, navigate to Displ…` (58 tokens) | `Thought: I should open Settings, go to Display, and set Brightness…` (46 tokens) |
| MAI-UI-2B **Q4_K_M** (1.11 GB) | `<thinking>\n<thinking>\n<thinking>\n</thinking>…` (hit the cap) | same (hit the cap) |

Q4_K_M behaviour depends on tiny input changes (704x1568, 768x1696 or a JPEG-recompressed copy of the same screenshot
were fine), i.e. the first token after `<thinking>` sits on a knife edge after 4-bit quantization. GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (same
Qwen3-VL architecture) and LFM3 v4 do not show this at Q4_K_M. Both GGUFs were converted from Tongyi-MAI/MAI-UI-2B @
5030509 with llama.cpp cd959bae9; the chat template is the standard Qwen3-VL one.

Decision: MAI-UI's AndroidWorld arm runs at **Q8_0** (everything else matched: one screenshot <= 1,048,576 px, temperature
0, same server flags). This gives MAI-UI a precision advantage over the Q4_K_M v4 and GUI-Owl arms; it is reported as
such. The smoke check now also fails if more than a quarter of the steps have an empty `<thinking>`.
     1	#!/bin/bash
     2	# Runs ON a benchmark host (GCP VM): for each model, start llama-server with the same flags as its evaluations
     3	# (CPU, -t THREADS, -np 1), run eval/mobileworld/bench_speed.py, then parse that server's per-request timings and RSS.
     4	# One model at a time on an otherwise idle machine. Usage: THREADS=8 bash bench_speed.sh > bench.log 2>&1
     5	set -u
     6	cd ~
     7	T=${THREADS:-8}; OUT=~/bench/results_t$T; mkdir -p "$OUT"
     8	S=llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server
     9	run() {  # name agent port server-args...
    10	  local name=$1 agent=$2 port=$3; shift 3
    11	  $S "$@" -np 1 -t "$T" --port "$port" --host 127.0.0.1 > "$OUT/server_$name.log" 2>&1 &
    12	  local pid=$!
    13	  until curl -s --max-time 5 127.0.0.1:$port/health | grep -q ok; do sleep 2; done
    14	  (cd MobileWorld && .venv/bin/python ~/lfm3/bench_speed.py --agent "$agent" --url "http://127.0.0.1:$port/v1" \
    15	      --shots ~/bench/shots --reps "${REPS:-3}" --out "$OUT/$name.json") > "$OUT/client_$name.log" 2>&1
    16	  echo "$name rss_mb $(( $(ps -o rss= -p $pid) / 1024 ))" >> "$OUT/rss.txt"
    17	  kill $pid; wait $pid 2>/dev/null
    18	}
    19	run v4 lfm3 8114 -m models/LFM3-VL-2B-AndroidAgent-v4-Q4_K_M.gguf --mmproj models/mmproj-LFM3-VL-2B-Q8_0.gguf \
    20	  -c 8192 --image-max-tokens 1024 --reasoning-format deepseek
    21	run guiowl guiowl 8092 -m models/GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct.Q4_K_M.gguf --mmproj models/GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct.mmproj-Q8_0.gguf \
    22	  -c 20480 --image-max-tokens 2600 --jinja
    23	run maiui maiui 8093 -m models/MAI-UI-2B-Q4_K_M.gguf --mmproj models/mmproj-MAI-UI-2B-Q8_0.gguf \
    24	  -c 20480 --image-max-tokens 2600 --jinja
    25	echo BENCH_DONE
     1	"""Per-step speed of the three 2B agents on identical inputs, through the same agent code used for evaluation.
     2	
     3	  lfm3   : eval/mobileworld/lfm3_mw_agent.py (v4 prompt, one screenshot, af.MAX_PIXELS resize, thinking on)
     4	  guiowl : MobileWorld's official GUI-Owl-1.5 agent (history_n=1 default)
     5	  maiui  : MobileWorld's official MAI-UI agent with history_n=1 (eval/mobileworld/maiui_1img_agent.py)
     6	
     7	Each call is the first step of a fresh episode on one of N real 1080x2400 MobileWorld screenshots with that task's real
     8	goal; one warm-up call is excluded. End-to-end latency = agent.predict() wall time (prompt building, image encoding to
     9	base64, HTTP, model, parsing). Server-side prompt/generation timings are read afterwards from the llama-server log
    10	(scripts/speed/bench_speed.sh). Usage (MobileWorld venv):
    11	  python bench_speed.py --agent lfm3 --url http://127.0.0.1:8114/v1 --shots ~/bench/shots --reps 3 --out res.json
    12	"""
    13	import argparse
    14	import glob
    15	import json
    16	import os
    17	import sys
    18	import time
    19	
    20	from PIL import Image, ImageOps
    21	
    22	p = argparse.ArgumentParser()
    23	p.add_argument("--agent", required=True, choices=["lfm3", "guiowl", "maiui"])
    24	p.add_argument("--url", required=True)
    25	p.add_argument("--shots", required=True)
    26	p.add_argument("--reps", type=int, default=3)
    27	p.add_argument("--out", required=True)
    28	p.add_argument("--jsonl", default="", help="also append each call to this file (fsync) as it completes")
    29	p.add_argument("--mirror_warmup", action="store_true",
    30	               help="warm up on a mirrored copy of the first screenshot so no timed call repeats the warm-up prompt")
    31	p.add_argument("--client_timeout", type=float, default=0,
    32	               help="if >0: OpenAI client timeout in seconds and max_retries=0 (slow phones; MobileWorld's default is 120 s with "
    33	                    "2 automatic re-sends, which queue duplicate requests on a single-slot server)")
    34	p.add_argument("--agent_dir", default="", help="directory holding lfm3_mw_agent.py / maiui_1img_agent.py / agent_format.py")
    35	a = p.parse_args()
    36	sys.path.insert(0, os.path.expanduser(a.agent_dir or "~/lfm3"))
    37	
    38	from mobile_world.tasks.registry import TaskRegistry  # noqa: E402
    39	
    40	reg = TaskRegistry()
    41	
    42	
    43	def make():
    44	    if a.agent == "lfm3":
    45	        from lfm3_mw_agent import LFM3MobileWorldAgent
    46	        return LFM3MobileWorldAgent(model_name="local", llm_base_url=a.url)
    47	    if a.agent == "guiowl":
    48	        from mobile_world.agents.implementations.gui_owl_1_5 import GUIOWL15AgentMCP
    49	        return GUIOWL15AgentMCP(model_name="GUI-Owl-1.5-2B", llm_base_url=a.url, tools=[])
    50	    from maiui_1img_agent import MAIUI1ImageAgent
    51	    return MAIUI1ImageAgent(llm_base_url=a.url, model_name="MAI-UI-2B")
    52	
    53	
    54	shots = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(a.shots), "*.png")))
    55	cases = []
    56	for f in shots:
    57	    task = os.path.basename(f).split("-")[0]
    58	    cases.append((task, reg.get_task(task).goal, Image.open(f).convert("RGB")))
    59	rows = []
    60	for rep in range(a.reps + 1):  # rep 0 = warm-up (first case only)
    61	    for i, (task, goal, img) in enumerate(cases if rep else cases[:1]):
    62	        if rep == 0 and a.mirror_warmup:
    63	            img = ImageOps.mirror(img)
    64	        ag = make()
    65	        if a.client_timeout > 0 and getattr(ag, "openai_client", None) is not None:
    66	            ag.openai_client = ag.openai_client.with_options(timeout=a.client_timeout, max_retries=0)
    67	        ag.initialize(goal)
    68	        t0 = time.time()
    69	        res = ag.predict({"screenshot": img, "tool_call": None, "ask_user_response": None})
    70	        dt = time.time() - t0
    71	        action = res[-1]
    72	        raw = res[0] if isinstance(res[0], str) else str(res[0])
    73	        rows.append({"rep": rep, "task": task, "latency_s": round(dt, 3), "raw_chars": len(raw),
    74	                     "action": action.model_dump(exclude_none=True) if hasattr(action, "model_dump") else str(action)})
    75	        print(json.dumps(rows[-1])[:200], flush=True)
    76	        if a.jsonl:
    77	            with open(a.jsonl, "a") as fh:
    78	                fh.write(json.dumps({"agent": a.agent, "t": time.time(), **rows[-1]}) + "\n")
    79	                fh.flush()
