results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:1:**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS.** The saved artifacts reproduce the preregistered primary result: v4 is non-inferior to matched GUI-Owl at the −6.9 pp margin, under the specified rerun and nominal inference rules. Superiority over GUI-Owl is not established. No P1 defect or erroneous primary count was substantiated. Device-state isolation is imperfect, one reference-arm success has a destructive extra action, and the analysis input guard is weaker than its identity claim.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:7:- **P2-1 — App snapshot restoration was skipped, so equal device configuration does not establish equal starting state.** `task_eval.py:116–125` catches snapshot restoration errors and proceeds. `app_snapshot.py:91–107` raises before clearing/copying app data when the snapshot is missing. The v4/1234 rerun log contains **263** “Snapshot not found” skips; ordinary full runs show approximately 271–275, across both devices and all arms. This is a shared harness limitation, not a special change benefiting the reruns. Actual state carryover is visible: v1/2026 attempts to create Thomas Pereira at 10:21, and that contact is still present in OpenAppTaskEval at 11:21. Evidence: [log at contact creation](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:10174), [later skipped restore](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:50476), [trajectory](trajectory_80_1.jpg), [all snapshot warnings with locations](execution_logs.json). Task-specific DB clearing and Clock resets still run; this does **not** mean every generated task state was wrong. It does mean preferences/residual state and episode order are not fully controlled, including when 113 episodes move to the other device. Neither the direction nor magnitude of resulting bias can be identified from these artifacts. Disclose this limitation; future runs need verified state restoration. Cross-template carryover is also outside what clustering only by template can account for.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:13:- **P3-2 — Two execution descriptions need correction; scores are unaffected.** The [16:20 entry](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:289) calls both VLC rerun crashes “in an agent step.” Their saved tracebacks instead show `episode_runner.py:76 -> agent.reset`, before its step loop. They still correctly count as failures because their one rerun was exhausted. Also, [13:40](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:276) promises exclusion of three **templates**, whereas published sensitivity B excludes seven individual **pairs**. The 16:20 description of B is accurate. I computed the literal three-template exclusion too: **54 versus 43 over 339 pairs/113 clusters**, +3.245 pp, CI [−3.030, 9.524], p 0.3655; NI remains established. See [tracebacks](exceptions.json) and [numbers](numbers.md).
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:27:The 78 goal-text-varying templates give v4 **32/234**, GUI-Owl **33/234**, difference **−0.427 pp**, CI **[−8.108, 7.207]**: NI is **not** established for that subgroup. This does not overturn the preregistered all-template endpoint. Constant goal text also does not imply invariant hidden task state: the source manifest distinguishes 20 such templates. Seed 30 remains development data and is not pooled into the held-out result.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:40:The **117 newly rerun originals qualify**, including all 113 v4/1234 device-setup crashes. BrowserDraw had already reached agent steps; the two specified SMS exceptions occurred in `is_successful`; all three correctly remain failures. All 122 reruns, including seed 7, have one logged start and one saved result each. Guards never fired. v1/2026's initial emulator-2 attempt had zero episodes, so the unchanged full relaunch on emulator 1 was legitimate. Every arm/device assignment, pause and resume is recorded in [execution_review.md](execution_review.md).
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:46:The nine changed goals are all explained by `InformationRetrieval.initialize_task`: parent device setup occurs before seeded `_maybe_replace_date` at line 85. Every one matches both other arms' goal, has the correct saved instance seed, and **fails**, so admitting these nine does not add any success. All 1,037 stored instance seeds and all 1,166 instance IDs validate; exception files omit the seed and full hidden parameter dictionaries are not saved. The diff from `dd2f7f7` changes only the stated goal admission/annotation and stale “pending” note; statistical/scoring logic is unchanged. Details and all nine text changes are in the execution review.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:1:**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS — as a preliminary, preregistered benchmark-checker result.** The final recorded scores and retry substitutions reproduce. Seed 7 does **not** establish non-inferiority, superiority, or equivalence. One v4 success contradicts its trajectory, and the “seed-varying” subset is misdefined. The reported 18 successes must not be described as 18 independently verified task completions.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:11:Impact: changing just this score to failure gives **v4 17/116 versus GUI-Owl 16/116**, difference **+0.862 pp**, exact McNemar **p=1**, and continuous sign-flip interval **[−8.065, +9.804] pp**. Non-inferiority still fails. Preserve the preregistered checker score with this disclosure and publish the sensitivity separately; do not silently rewrite the primary endpoint.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:13:**P2-2 — goal-string comparison is not a seed-varying-template classifier.** [Analysis lines 113–119](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/sealed_analysis.py:113) correctly find **76 observed goal changes** between seeds 30 and 7, but label these as the preregistered varying templates. Two potentially varying goals happen to collide: `OpenAppTaskEval` chooses **contacts** in both seeds; `SportsTrackerLongestDistanceActivity` chooses **mountain biking** in both. The latter's sampled distance changes from **1200 to 4500 meters** despite identical wording. Adding these two yields the **78 templates whose goals can vary**, with final scores **11/78, 14/78, 5/78** for v4/GUI-Owl/v1, instead of **10/76, 14/76, 4/76**.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:21:The 4-v4/1-GUI exception split does **not** establish emulator-2 or shared-adb load as its cause. Both use server port 5037 with explicit device serials; both original logs contain adb/SIGTRAP failures. The local controller suppresses shared-server restarts, and the reviewed logs record no restart. GUI-Owl/v1 log filtering removes fork-warning lines, so raw warning counts cannot be compared with v4's unfiltered log. No contemporaneous load/isolation record proves or excludes interference from other jobs. The prescribed retries replace all five exception records; four remain failures and GUI-Owl gains one success. Do not claim either a clean infrastructure run or a demonstrated v4-favoring load bias.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:51:Secondary exceptions-dropped results before retries: **18/112, 15/115, 11/116**; the paired analysis correctly retains only **111 common nonexception pairs**, 15/10 discordants, difference +4.504505 pp, McNemar 0.424356. After substitution, all 116 pairs are nonexceptional, so secondary equals primary. Complete before/after numbers, including all reference comparisons, are in [recomputed.json](recomputed.json) and [interval_recomputed.json](interval_recomputed.json).
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:65:All five traces go through `suite_utils.py:245 task.initialize_task`, before `run_episode` at line 247. **Eligibility is established by stack location, not empty episode data**: `_create_failed_result` discards steps for any caught exception. Each supplied retry contains exactly one new episode per eligible task; all five replace their originals, including all four failed retries. This follows the once-only rule.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:73:Original local times on November 18: GUI-Owl **01:35–09:30**, emulator 5556; v1 **01:30–06:32**, emulator 5558; v4 **13:22–18:07**, emulator 5558. Each original log has one run start/end and no checkpoint-resume/skipped-task marker; episode timestamps do not show a pause/restart. The preregistered possibility of pausing v1 is not evidence it actually occurred. Initial preregistration commit `29d5d25` predates the first launch, despite the approximate time in its heading.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:75:The first runner used by GUI-Owl/v1 differs from v4's later runner in logging/startup/exit handling. The resume/atomic-checkpoint changes do not give a saved seed-7 episode another attempt. Both primary arms receive the same app-list construction, one screenshot, temperature 0, one-second post-action waits and `int(10 × complexity)` steps. [Static budget and episode checks](execution_checks.json) find no over-budget episode across originals/retries. The actual per-episode app-list text was not persisted, so exact installed-package equality cannot be proved from the episodes.
