results/codex/session_1118_audit/report.md:79:Given the reported 14:09 GUI-Owl OOM, invalidating `guiowl_gui_en` and starting a **fresh full** `guiowl_gui_en_r2` is correct; do not retain its four successes or stitch attempts. The raw Colab OOM/r2 startup logs were not available in the inspected local artifacts, so that incident and current remote flags remain user-supplied premises. The checked-in launcher still omits the reported recovery flag `--cache-ram 0` (`scripts/colab_mw_models.sh:17–22`); record the actual restart command/configuration for reproducibility.
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:37:Input design matters most where our failures sit: noticing that an action did nothing. SecAgent-3B's offline ablation is the clearest small-model evidence. Adding one previous screenshot raised task accuracy from **36.2 to 72.8** for 45% more input tokens, with little further gain at five, and removing the natural-language "semantic context" summary cut the one-screenshot result to 56.4 ([SecAgent](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.08533)). OpenPhone-3B fell from 15.2 to 4.3 on AndroidLab without history ([OpenPhone](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.22009)). Resolution is a smaller, secondary factor. MAI-UI found 720p matches 1080p while 540p "substantially degrades" performance ([MAI-UI](https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.22047)), and our 774K-pixel budget (about 590×1310 on a 1080×2400 screen, ~720 image tokens) sits at the low end of that range. Prompt order is a free rider: Phi-Ground measured +1.7 to +2.4 on mobile grounding from putting the instruction before the image ([Phi-Ground](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.23779)), and our prompt places the image first ([agent_format.py](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/train/agent_format.py)).
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:39:Short reasoning should stay, and action-only rows are a risk. Ferret-UI Lite-3B went from 13.7 on AW with no CoT to 15.8 with short and 19.6 with long CoT ([Ferret-UI Lite](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.26539)), and GUI-Libra-3B fell from 25.2 to 12.2 without CoT ([GUI-Libra](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.22190)). At 4B, MIRAGE's **action-only SFT (31.0) scored below the untuned base (42.9)** ([MIRAGE](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04627)). That is a warning for v2, whose 7,469 AMEX rows have blank intents rendered as empty `<think></think>` ([v2 card](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/data_v2/README.md)).
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:44:| Recovery injection and loop-label masking | GUI-Reflection 8B: 14.6→23.6 on its own env ([GUI-Reflection](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.08012)); Xiaomi-GUI-0 masking ([Xiaomi-GUI-0](https://arxiv.org/html/2606.31410v2)) | +1 to +4 | SFT only | Step 2 |
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:55:The estimate column extrapolates from 3-8B Qwen-family results. No paper reports any of these levers on an LFM-style hybrid conv/attention backbone, and gains from different levers will overlap rather than add.
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:59:The budget decides the method. At about 10 compute units per G4-hour, the remaining ~25 + ~10 Colab units come to **about 3.5 G4-hours**. Modal's ~$13 covers roughly one more v1-sized run, since v1 LFM3 and the 450M run together used about $13 on Modal ([project memory](/Users/alpha/.claude/projects/-Users-alpha-lfm3-android/memory/lfm3-android-agent-project.md)). Qwen3.5-0.8B trains at 1.8 s/step on the G4 ([STATUS](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/STATUS.md)), so a 1,250-step 2B run plus evals should take about an hour, or about 1.5 hours with a second image (estimate). That allows three training runs and a small evaluation-and-generation session, not an RL campaign.
docs/research/small-gui-agent-training-methods.md:72:**Step 2, the first training run,** carries the cheap, well-evidenced data fixes. It needs no new infrastructure and keeps the current single-image format. The largest piece is navigate-then-answer episodes: rewrite held AC and GUI-Odyssey goals into questions whose answer is visible on the final screenshot, as Ferret-UI Lite and OpenMobile do, and end each episode with `answer(...)` followed by `status complete`. UI-Venus rebuilt its information-retrieval traces the same way to insert explicit answers ([UI-Venus](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10833)). v2's ScreenQA rows teach the `answer` format only on single screens, so they do not cover this pattern. No-op recovery needs no emulator either. GUI-Reflection built its "ineffective action" samples from AndroidControl: add an action that cannot change the screen (a scroll at a list boundary, a tap on blank space) to the history, keep the same screenshot, and keep the gold action as the label ([GUI-Reflection](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.08012)). Loop masking removes the labels on consecutive identical actions and on `wait` runs while keeping those steps in the history, because Xiaomi-GUI-0 found that using repeated steps as labels "teaches the model … to keep repeating when stuck" ([Xiaomi-GUI-0](https://arxiv.org/html/2606.31410v2)). Finally, compute the screen difference between consecutive gold screenshots and write into the training history the same "[no visible change]" note the runtime harness already produces, so the note stops being a test-time surprise. GUI-Libra-style upweighting of action tokens is an optional, cheap addition; expect less than its 3B gain, because our thoughts are already short.
results/codex/round2_audit/report.md:109:The option-2 conclusion is **robust within the measured pilot**: GUI-Owl is **4.792–5.239×**, and MAI-UI **4.431–4.895×**, slower than v4 on **every paired screenshot/pass**. Reversing order changes the model medians only slightly. No thermal adjustment is needed to preserve that observed ranking. Generalization to other workloads/devices or perfectly controlled temperatures is not established.
results/codex/round2_audit/report.md:148:All **12** combinations of direction and portrait/landscape/odd-sized test dimensions passed the coordinate comparison. Evidence: `lfm3_mw_agent.py:99–101,127–131`; `AW/env/actuation.py:138–167`; `MW/core/server.py:386–390`; `MW/runtime/controller.py:248–255`. This resolves the former reversed horizontal direction and shortened travel distance.
results/codex/round2_audit/report.md:152:* AndroidWorld uses **`env.logical_screen_size`** (`AW/env/interface.py:306–311,345–347`); the adapter uses the **original observation screenshot's `.size`**, before model resizing. MobileWorld retrieves the screenshot without resizing in its client (`MW/runtime/client.py:112–132`), and its drag passes the adapter's coordinates unchanged. Matching full-screen screenshot/logical dimensions gives matching geometry. No run-2 screenshot/display metadata was available to prove that equality on the remote container; no mismatch is demonstrated either.
results/codex/round2_audit/report.md:184:SPEED also repeats **Q1/Q2/Q4** at lines **29,31,41,52,75–76**. Fix the QDC report generator and SPEED template's cache explanation; merely regenerating the current inputs reproduces those errors.
results/codex/round2_audit/report.md:215:The reviewed SPEED/EVALUATIONS files and their registry expose seed-1234 **file counts** and protocol metadata, not outcomes; seed-2026 remains protocol-only. Their only held-out outcome table comes from the authorized seed-7 analysis. `scripts/build_runs_registry.py:181–186` counts sealed filenames; its outcome-reading calls use explicit unsealed roots and the seed-7 analysis text (`:225–231`). The registry builder was not executed. Counts for still-sealed arms were not independently inspected. No sealed result, answer, trajectory, or forbidden log was opened or found leaked in these reviewed docs.
