     1	# How the benchmarks were run
     2	
     3	**Contents:** [Fairness at a glance](#fairness-at-a-glance) · [AndroidWorld](#androidworld) ·
     4	[MobileWorld](#mobileworld) · [AndroidControl](#androidcontrol-offline) ·
     5	[General knowledge](#general-knowledge-retention) · [Speed](#speed)
     6	
     7	---
     8	
     9	## Fairness at a glance
    10	
    11	| Matched across compared models | Not matched (disclosed) |
    12	|---|---|
    13	| Same harness, emulator image, tasks and seeds | Image size: AndroidWorld v4 ≤ 880×880 px area (≈ 720 tokens) vs GUI-Owl / MAI-UI ≤ 1,048,576 px (≈ 1,024 tokens); MobileWorld v4 the same vs full screenshots up to 2,600 tokens (favours them) |
    14	| One screenshot per step | Prompt and output format: each model uses its own |
    15	| Same step budget, temperature 0 | GUI-Owl is not in its published 5-screenshot setup |
    16	| 4-bit weights via llama.cpp (MAI-UI: 8-bit, its 4-bit output breaks) | GUI-Owl's / MAI-UI's AndroidWorld training exposure is undisclosed |
    17	| Installed-app list in the prompt for both v4 and GUI-Owl (held-out runs) | Parse retries: v4 one retry; GUI-Owl's unparseable reply wastes the step |
    18	| Exceptions count as failures for everyone | v4 trained with **no** AndroidWorld data (contamination rule) |
    19	
    20	Why GUI-Owl runs with one screenshot: its native setup (current + 4 previous screenshots at full resolution) took
    21	61 s per step on the M5 (~10,700 prompt tokens). A full 116-task run would take about two days per seed. The
    22	on-device budget this project targets is one screenshot.
    23	
    24	---
    25	
    26	## AndroidWorld
    27	
    28	### Setup (all models)
    29	
    30	| Item | Setting |
    31	|---|---|
    32	| Benchmark | AndroidWorld @ `55ddaf5` + local patches (below); 116 task templates, 1 instance each |
    33	| Device | Pixel 6 AVD, Android 13 (API 33, arm64); two emulators (ports 5556, 5558) on an Apple M5 Mac |
    34	| Model server | llama.cpp `llama-server` on Metal, one request at a time |
    35	| Weights | 4-bit (Q4_K_M) + 8-bit image projector; MAI-UI 8-bit (Q8_0) |
    36	| Step budget | AndroidWorld default: 10 × task complexity |
    37	| Decoding | Temperature 0 |
    38	| Seeds | Development: 30. Held-out: 7, 1234, 2026 |
    39	| Success | Checker score ≥ 1 **and** the agent ended the episode. Exceptions are failures |
    40	
    41	### Per-model settings (held-out runs)
    42	
    43	| | v4 | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (matched) | v1 |
    44	|---|---|---|---|
    45	| Agent code | `eval/androidworld/lfm_agent.py`, prompt v4 | `eval/androidworld/guiowl_agent.py` (official prompt, ported) | `lfm_agent.py`, original prompt |
    46	| Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 | 1 |
    47	| Image | ≤ 880×880 px area (≈ 720 tokens; server cap 1,024) | ≤ 1,048,576 px (≈ 1,024 tokens; server cap 2,600 not reached) | as v4 |
    48	| Context window | 8,192 | 20,480 | 8,192 |
    49	| Installed-app list | yes | yes | no |
    50	| Output | `<think>intent</think>` + one JSON action | `Action:` + `<tool_call>` | as v4 |
    51	
    52	Launcher with the exact flags: [`scripts/androidworld/local_sealed_aw_v3.sh`](../scripts/androidworld/local_sealed_aw_v3.sh).
    53	
    54	### Local patches to AndroidWorld
    55	
    56	Files: `eval/androidworld/android_world_local_fixes.patch`, `eval/androidworld/android_env_no_adb_kill.patch`.
    57	None touches model input/output or scoring.
    58	
    59	- App launch works on software-key emulators (`monkey --pct-syskeys 0`).
    60	- The shared adb server is never killed; optional adb server port.
    61	- Directory cleanup is verified; a failed cleanup fails the attempt.
    62	- A crash in `tear_down` is recorded on the episode instead of stopping the suite.
    63	- Resume keeps saved exception episodes as failures; checkpoints are written atomically.
    64	
    65	### Held-out protocol (preregistered)
    66	
    67	- **Sealed:** results went to `results/androidworld_sealed/`; only episode counts were checked until every model
    68	  had finished that seed.
    69	- **Re-run rule:** an infrastructure crash before step 1 (emulator/adb, not model output) is re-run once.
    70	  Everything else counts as it is.
    71	- **Trajectory review:** every checker success is compared with its saved screenshots. Contradicted successes are
    72	  listed in `results/aw_checker_disputes.json` and enter only a sensitivity analysis.
    73	- **Primary analysis:** paired difference v4 − GUI-Owl over 348 instances; template-clustered sign-flip test
    74	  (10,000 draws, seed 0); 95% CI by test inversion.
    75	- **Decision rule:** non-inferior if the CI's lower bound is above −6.9 points (8 tasks of 116).
    76	- **Development gate:** v4 had to pass a gate on seed 30 and offline checks before it could run held-out. It passed.
    77	
    78	Full text and every dated change: [PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md).
    79	
    80	---
    81	
    82	## MobileWorld
    83	
    84	| Item | Setting |
    85	|---|---|
    86	| Benchmark | MobileWorld @ `a026188`, 105 English GUI-only tasks |
    87	| Environment | Official Docker image (`ghcr.io/tongyi-mai/mobile_world`), on a GCP n2-standard-16 spot VM with nested virtualisation |
    88	| Model servers | llama.cpp `cd959bae9` on a Colab T4 GPU, reached through a restricted reverse SSH tunnel |
    89	| Task settings | 50 rounds, 3 s step wait, `--auto_retry 3`, temperature 0 |
    90	| v4 agent | Our adapter: `eval/mobileworld/lfm3_mw_agent.py` |
    91	| GUI-Owl agent | MobileWorld's official `gui_owl_1_5` agent |
    92	| MAI-UI agent | MobileWorld's official agent, 1 screenshot (`eval/mobileworld/maiui_mw_agent.py`) |
    93	
    94	**Completion rule** (fixed 2026-11-19 01:55, before any re-run outcome; in
    95	[`scripts/mobileworld/gcp_mw_resume_vm.sh`](../scripts/mobileworld/gcp_mw_resume_vm.sh)):
    96	
    97	| Task ended because… | Handling |
    98	|---|---|
    99	| Setup or scoring failed (HTTP 500 from the environment) | One more invocation in a freshly restarted container (up to 4 executions inside it) |
   100	| VM stop or preemption cut it off, or never reached | Run it |
   101	| Model server unreachable (added before MAI-UI started) | Run it |
   102	| Unsupported action, unparseable output, `ask_user` without a simulator | Failure |
   103	
   104	MAI-UI ran in two halves (53/52 tasks, alternating) in parallel containers, after GUI-Owl and v4 had finished.
   105	
   106	---
   107	
   108	## AndroidControl (offline)
   109	
   110	| Item | Setting |
   111	|---|---|
   112	| Data | Official **test** episodes: 1,543 episodes, 8,444 steps |
   113	| Modes | High-level (goal + history → action; headline), low-level (+ step instruction), terminal rows (→ `complete`) |
   114	| History | Teacher-forced (human step instructions + ground-truth actions); an upper bound on closed-loop behaviour |
   115	| Generation | Greedy, ≤ 256 new tokens, bf16 on GPU (`eval/androidcontrol/generate.py`) |
   116	| Scoring | `eval/androidcontrol/score.py`; unparseable output = wrong |
   117	
   118	Step success rate counts a step correct if the action type matches and:
   119	
   120	| Action | Correct if |
   121	|---|---|
   122	| click, long_press | Point inside the target element's box, or within 14% of the screen of the true point |
   123	| input_text | Normalised exact match or token F1 ≥ 0.5 |
   124	| scroll | Same direction |
   125	| open_app | Case-insensitive match or containment |
   126	| back, home, wait | Type match is enough |
   127	
   128	Development splits (GUI-Odyssey, AMEX, ScreenQA, v4 questions) use the same scorer; see [datasets.md](datasets.md).
   129	
   130	---
   131	
   132	## General knowledge (retention)
   133	
   134	- MMStar (1,500 questions) and MMLU (1,000), forced-choice next-token scoring (independent of output format).
   135	- Each fine-tune is compared with its base model on the same questions (paired, exact McNemar).
   136	- Code: `eval/general/eval_general.py`, `eval/general/paired_retention.py`.
   137	
   138	---
   139	
   140	## Speed
   141	
   142	| Measurement | How |
   143	|---|---|
   144	| CPU | Idle GCP n2-standard-16, 8 threads. 5 real screenshots and goals through each model's own evaluation agent, 1 warm-up + 3 passes. Calls served from llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache are excluded. Script: [`scripts/speed/bench_speed.sh`](../scripts/speed/bench_speed.sh) |
   145	| Apple M5 | Model time per step recorded inside the AndroidWorld seed-30 runs, while emulators and other servers were running |
   146	| Phone | Qualcomm reference phone (Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6) via Qualcomm Device Cloud. llama.cpp b12110 runs **on the phone's CPU** (4 threads, RAM cache off); the Mac sends screenshots through each model's own agent. Files checked by SHA-256. Scripts: [`scripts/speed/qdc_chain2.sh`](../scripts/speed/qdc_chain2.sh) |
   147	
   148	Phone caveats:
   149	- Frequencies are sampled, not controlled.
   150	- GUI-Owl and MAI-UI reused cached system-prompt tokens, which favours them.
   151	- v4's agent sends a 576×1280 screenshot; the others send 1080×2400.
     1	# Infrastructure and incidents
     2	
     3	**Contents:** [Where things ran](#where-things-ran) · [Cost controls](#cost-controls) · [Incidents](#incidents-and-fixes) ·
     4	[Lessons](#lessons)
     5	
     6	---
     7	
     8	## Where things ran
     9	
    10	| Work | Hardware |
    11	|---|---|
    12	| SFT v1, v3, LFM2.5-VL-450M | Modal GPU containers (A100 / H100) |
    13	| SFT Qwen3.5-2B / 0.8B, v2 mixes | Google Colab GPUs |
    14	| SFT v4, offline evals, v4-RL (GRPO) | Colab A100-40GB (about 31 compute units) |
    15	| AndroidWorld: every seed-30 and held-out run | Apple M5 Mac, 2 Android emulators (Pixel 6, API 33, arm64), llama.cpp on Metal |
    16	| MobileWorld v4 run 1 (discarded) | AWS EC2 `c8i.4xlarge` (nested virtualisation), model on CPU |
    17	| MobileWorld run 2: GUI-Owl, v4, MAI-UI | GCP `n2-standard-16` spot VM (nested virtualisation); models on a Colab T4 through a reverse SSH tunnel restricted to the model ports |
    18	| CPU speed benchmark | The same GCP VM, idle, before its MobileWorld run |
    19	| Phone speed benchmark | Qualcomm Device Cloud (Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 reference phone); earlier attempt on a Pixel 9 via Firebase device streaming |
    20	| Audits and research | Codex CLI on the Mac |
    21	
    22	Colab VMs have no KVM, so Android emulators could not run there. That is why MobileWorld moved to AWS and GCP.
    23	
    24	---
    25	
    26	## Cost controls
    27	
    28	- Every cloud VM powers itself off after 12 h (AWS `shutdown -h`, GCP `--max-run-duration`).
    29	- Colab sessions were stopped by a watchdog once their jobs finished.
    30	- The whole pipeline was smoke-tested before any paid run (rule adopted after an early v3 attempt failed inside a
    31	  paid pipeline).
    32	
    33	---
    34	
    35	## Incidents and fixes
    36	
    37	| When (Manila) | Incident | Handling |
    38	|---|---|---|
    39	| 11-16/17 | Early v3 attempt failed inside its paid pipeline | Rule: smoke-test the whole pipeline before paid compute |
    40	| 11-17 | v2 scored 3/116 | Diagnosed as blank intents with a forced-intent ablation; fixed in v3 |
    41	| 11-18 04:51 | Colab A100 VM lost during v4 SFT (step 353) | Resumed from the step-350 Hub checkpoint on a new A100; training refuses to restart from scratch if a checkpoint exists |
    42	| 11-18 06:25 | Answer check accepted padded answers ("12M is incorrect") | Stricter gate criterion, fixed before any v4 result |
    43	| 11-18 08:10 | Hugging Face private storage full; merged v4 upload failed | Weights copied off the VM and verified tensor by tensor; the v2 dataset was made public to free space |
    44	| 11-18 09:30 | Resuming an AndroidWorld run would retry saved exceptions | Patched: saved failures stay failures; checkpoints written atomically |
    45	| 11-18 11:20 | GUI-Owl on CPU ≈ 45–58 s per step | Served from a Colab GPU through a tunnel |
    46	| 11-18 13:50 | llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache served repeated screenshots in the speed test | Cached calls excluded from the statistics |
    47	| 11-18 14:09 | GUI-Owl's MobileWorld model server killed by out-of-memory (prompt cache) | Run 1 discarded; run 2 with `--cache-ram 0` |
    48	| 11-19 00:35–08:06 | Emulator 2 hung; 113 v4 seed-1234 episodes crashed in setup | Preregistered single re-run on emulator 1 with a liveness guard ([`aw_emu_guard.sh`](../scripts/androidworld/aw_emu_guard.sh)) |
    49	| 11-19 04:57 | GCP VM stopped at its 12-h limit; MobileWorld containers vanished (`docker run --rm`) | Containers recreated with the original command |
    50	| 11-19 10:30 | Restarted container's emulator refused to boot (stale AVD locks) | Graceful emulator stop + lock cleanup before every restart |
    51	| 11-19 12:40 | First Colab model session hit its 24-h limit | Failover session with identical files (SHA-256), build and flags took over in 1 s |
    52	| 11-19 12:42, 14:29 | Two spot-VM preemptions during MAI-UI's run | Watcher restarted the VM, recreated containers, re-ran interrupted tasks |
    53	| 11-19 (MAI-UI run) | Emulators died 17 times with a fatal KVM error | Disclosed; affected tasks reported as a sensitivity analysis |
    54	
    55	Full details and timing: dated entries in [PREREG_v4.md](PREREG_v4.md).
    56	
    57	---
    58	
    59	## Lessons
    60	
    61	| Lesson | Applied as |
    62	|---|---|
    63	| Episode counts hide total failure | Watch exception counts and emulator liveness during sealed runs, not just progress |
    64	| `--rm` containers vanish on VM stop | Recreate containers from the original command; stop emulators gracefully |
    65	| Prompt caches distort speed and memory | Disable or exclude cached calls in benchmarks |
    66	| Paid runs fail late | Smoke-test the full pipeline first; persist outputs as you go |

