Counts: v4 17 + 19 = 36; GUI-Owl 13 + 18 = 31; v1 10 + 11 = 21. Retained 87; proposed dispute 1 (reference only). Existing seed-7 ClockStopWatchPausedVerify dispute is preserved separately in the published sensitivity and is not duplicated in the new proposals.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:1:**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS.** The saved artifacts reproduce the preregistered primary result: v4 is non-inferior to matched GUI-Owl at the −6.9 pp margin, under the specified rerun and nominal inference rules. Superiority over GUI-Owl is not established. No P1 defect or erroneous primary count was substantiated. Device-state isolation is imperfect, one reference-arm success has a destructive extra action, and the analysis input guard is weaker than its identity claim.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:3:Offline audit of all specified inputs, including the entire preregistration and every dated entry; 1,044 original episodes, 122 reruns, exception traces, execution/server/queue/guard logs, runners, agents and local harness patches. No AndroidWorld, emulator, llama-server or adb was run; no process was signalled. All writes are in this audit directory. [Independent code](recompute.py), [723 output checks](published_numeric_checks.json), [complete numerical tables](numbers.md), [execution review](execution_review.md), and [all 88 success reviews](success_review.md) provide the supporting detail.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:7:- **P2-1 — App snapshot restoration was skipped, so equal device configuration does not establish equal starting state.** `task_eval.py:116–125` catches snapshot restoration errors and proceeds. `app_snapshot.py:91–107` raises before clearing/copying app data when the snapshot is missing. The v4/1234 rerun log contains **263** “Snapshot not found” skips; ordinary full runs show approximately 271–275, across both devices and all arms. This is a shared harness limitation, not a special change benefiting the reruns. Actual state carryover is visible: v1/2026 attempts to create Thomas Pereira at 10:21, and that contact is still present in OpenAppTaskEval at 11:21. Evidence: [log at contact creation](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:10174), [later skipped restore](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:50476), [trajectory](trajectory_80_1.jpg), [all snapshot warnings with locations](execution_logs.json). Task-specific DB clearing and Clock resets still run; this does **not** mean every generated task state was wrong. It does mean preferences/residual state and episode order are not fully controlled, including when 113 episodes move to the other device. Neither the direction nor magnitude of resulting bias can be identified from these artifacts. Disclose this limitation; future runs need verified state restoration. Cross-template carryover is also outside what clustering only by template can account for.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:9:- **P2-2 — A reference-arm “open Contacts” success includes deleting a contact.** v1/2026 OpenAppTaskEval opens Contacts, selects all, presses trash, confirms deletion, then reports complete. The final screen says “No contacts yet” and “1 contact deleted.” [Source checker](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/single/system.py:484) checks only the foreground package, so the unrelated deletion is unpenalized. The literal open-app condition is satisfied, but this is not a clean user-level success. See [review #80](success_review.md) and [screens](trajectory_80_1.jpg). Added one proposal to [disputes_proposed.json](disputes_proposed.json); the original dispute file is untouched. Counting this proposal as failure changes v1 to **31/348**, and v4−v1 to **+6.61 pp**, CI **[1.54, 11.70]**, p **0.0119**. It does not affect v4−GUI-Owl.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:21:| v1 reference | 11 | 10 | 11 | 32/348 = 9.20% | 6.589–12.693 |
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:25:The correct preregistration reading is **116 template clusters, each containing its three seed instances** ([Analysis](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:39)). Treating 348 seed/template instances as independent clusters would discard the dependence the preregistration explicitly protects against. Per-seed v4-only/GUI-Owl-only/both counts are **15/13/3**, **13/9/4**, **11/10/8**; exact McNemar p values are **0.8505540**, **0.5234671**, **1.0**. All per-seed/pooled Wilson values, other comparisons, answer/action/difficulty breakdowns, secondary denominators and the seed-7 analysis reproduce; see [numbers.md](numbers.md).
