results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:40:The **117 newly rerun originals qualify**, including all 113 v4/1234 device-setup crashes. BrowserDraw had already reached agent steps; the two specified SMS exceptions occurred in `is_successful`; all three correctly remain failures. All 122 reruns, including seed 7, have one logged start and one saved result each. Guards never fired. v1/2026's initial emulator-2 attempt had zero episodes, so the unchanged full relaunch on emulator 1 was legitimate. Every arm/device assignment, pause and resume is recorded in [execution_review.md](execution_review.md).
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:42:The exhaustive midnight–10:05 emulator-2 timeline contains GUI-Owl/1234's last three episodes, five seed-7 reruns, v4/1234's 116 episodes, and the zero-episode v1 launch. The two pre-hang AudioRecorder failures have responsive screens and normal fetches; their actions do not justify an infrastructure exception. No additional saved episode was shown to be invalidated by the hang.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:46:The nine changed goals are all explained by `InformationRetrieval.initialize_task`: parent device setup occurs before seeded `_maybe_replace_date` at line 85. Every one matches both other arms' goal, has the correct saved instance seed, and **fails**, so admitting these nine does not add any success. All 1,037 stored instance seeds and all 1,166 instance IDs validate; exception files omit the seed and full hidden parameter dictionaries are not saved. The diff from `dd2f7f7` changes only the stated goal admission/annotation and stale “pending” note; statistical/scoring logic is unchanged. Details and all nine text changes are in the execution review.
results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md:50:Reviewed all **88** new-seed successes: v4 36, GUI-Owl 31, v1 21. All have a terminal action; none succeeds solely on budget exhaustion. One new proposal is described above; 87 have no sufficient contradiction in the saved evidence. The seed-1234 lemongrass recipe successes are vacuous zero-target instances permitted by the generator, not demonstrated false positives. The calendar deletion with a stale-looking final search list has an explicit delete confirmation and a DB-checker success; the screenshot alone is insufficient to dispute it. [The ledger](success_review.md) distinguishes these cases and the limits of inspecting screenshots without complete saved databases.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:1:**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS — as a preliminary, preregistered benchmark-checker result.** The final recorded scores and retry substitutions reproduce. Seed 7 does **not** establish non-inferiority, superiority, or equivalence. One v4 success contradicts its trajectory, and the “seed-varying” subset is misdefined. The reported 18 successes must not be described as 18 independently verified task completions.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:3:Audit scope: the three original seed-7 runs (348 episodes), five retries, seed-30 development comparison, all dated preregistration entries, analysis/runner/agent/checker sources and seed-7 logs. No other sealed result or log was opened. No AndroidWorld, emulator, model server, adb command or process signal was executed. All audit writes are in this directory.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:7:**P2-1 — v4 receives a false-positive stopwatch success.** In `v4_seed7/run_20261118T132321898379/ClockStopWatchPausedVerify_0.pkl.gz`, the goal is “Pause the stopwatch.” The four actions are open Clock → select Stopwatch → click Play → `status(complete)`. The terminal observation shows **02.99 and a Pause button**, with no subsequent pause action. The checker nevertheless logs `Start present: True`, `Stopwatch: 2`, then success. Its predicate accepts any `Start` accessibility node plus two Stopwatch nodes; the saved trajectory contradicts the accepted state. The checker-time accessibility tree was not recorded, so stale versus extraneous accessibility nodes cannot be distinguished.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:9:Evidence: [four-step image](ClockStopWatchPausedVerify_steps.jpg), [outputs/actions](success_traces.json), [last physical tap and checker log](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v4_seed7/run_output.SEALED.log:4591), [checker predicate](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/single/clock.py:43). The first teardown action follows the success log; teardown does not explain the mismatch.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:13:**P2-2 — goal-string comparison is not a seed-varying-template classifier.** [Analysis lines 113–119](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/sealed_analysis.py:113) correctly find **76 observed goal changes** between seeds 30 and 7, but label these as the preregistered varying templates. Two potentially varying goals happen to collide: `OpenAppTaskEval` chooses **contacts** in both seeds; `SportsTrackerLongestDistanceActivity` chooses **mountain biking** in both. The latter's sampled distance changes from **1200 to 4500 meters** despite identical wording. Adding these two yields the **78 templates whose goals can vary**, with final scores **11/78, 14/78, 5/78** for v4/GUI-Owl/v1, instead of **10/76, 14/76, 4/76**.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:15:Moreover, the remaining 38 are not all invariant *instances*: 20 have seeded hidden inputs/setup, including browser puzzles, receipt contents, duplicate recipes, and calendar/task-list queries with fixed wording. Counting seeded parameters/setup gives 98 templates under that broader definition. Thus **76 is right for this observed text comparison; 78 is defensible for potentially varying goal text; neither establishes that the other instances repeat unchanged**. The literature's [38/78 split](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.07432v1) does not supply a pinned manifest for this local implementation. This affects the generalization breakdown, not the 116-task primary score. Use an explicit, source-checked template manifest and state the definition.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:17:Evidence: [subset membership and scores](template_subsets.json), [independent parameter draws](ir_parameters_reconstructed.json), [reproduction/source catalog](subset_audit.py), [OpenApp generator](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/single/system.py:479), [sports task definition](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/information_retrieval/proto/tasks.textproto:2488).
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:21:The 4-v4/1-GUI exception split does **not** establish emulator-2 or shared-adb load as its cause. Both use server port 5037 with explicit device serials; both original logs contain adb/SIGTRAP failures. The local controller suppresses shared-server restarts, and the reviewed logs record no restart. GUI-Owl/v1 log filtering removes fork-warning lines, so raw warning counts cannot be compared with v4's unfiltered log. No contemporaneous load/isolation record proves or excludes interference from other jobs. The prescribed retries replace all five exception records; four remain failures and GUI-Owl gains one success. Do not claim either a clean infrastructure run or a demonstrated v4-favoring load bias.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:23:**P3-1 — the CI grid trims the accepted interval inward.** [Analysis lines 164–171](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/sealed_analysis.py:164) report the first/last accepted **0.1-pp grid points**, not the continuous inversion endpoints. Final primary **[−7.2, +10.7]** is actually **[−7.272727, +10.769231] pp** for the same 10,000 draws. Report continuous endpoints or round outward to **[−7.3, +10.8]**. This does not change the seed-7 decision. The permutation `+1` correction and endpoint indexing are correct; this is discretization, not an off-by-one episode error.
