results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:47:One seed means one observation per template: clustering does not change the 116 paired units. At zero, exact sign-flip equals exact McNemar; Monte Carlo differences are expected. Exact-enumeration inversion is identical to the final primary interval; v1−GUI-Owl's upper endpoint is 3.703704 pp under exact enumeration. The v4−v1 lower endpoint of zero is genuine discreteness, not evidence of superiority.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:49:Before retries, GUI-Owl was 15/116 (Wilson 7.9954–20.2431%), action 8/91, medium 5/36, varying-text 13/76; v4/v1 numerators were unchanged. Primary difference was +2.586207 pp, discordants 15/12, McNemar 0.701108, Monte Carlo p=0.707029; continuous Monte Carlo interval [−6.250000, +11.475410], exact interval [−6.349206, +11.475410]. The provisional NI “yes” becomes **“no”** after the valid GUI-Owl retry. Final lower bound −7.272727 is below −6.9; exact two-sided p at −6.9 is 0.061193. Using precisely −8/116 instead of rounded −6.9 pp does not alter this decision.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:51:Secondary exceptions-dropped results before retries: **18/112, 15/115, 11/116**; the paired analysis correctly retains only **111 common nonexception pairs**, 15/10 discordants, difference +4.504505 pp, McNemar 0.424356. After substitution, all 116 pairs are nonexceptional, so secondary equals primary. Complete before/after numbers, including all reference comparisons, are in [recomputed.json](recomputed.json) and [interval_recomputed.json](interval_recomputed.json).
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:53:**CI interpretation:** test inversion is a reasonable operational reading of [the preregistration](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:39), which names sign-flipping and a lower 95% bound but leaves inversion, tails, grid and RNG unspecified. It is **not an exact finite-sample 95% interval for a binary mean difference merely because its randomization distribution was enumerated exactly**. Away from zero, flipping `d−delta` requires a symmetry/exchangeability justification beyond the mean-null; ternary differences shifted by −6.9 pp do not satisfy that symmetry automatically. Treat this as a nominal sign-flip interval with an explicit assumption, not guaranteed coverage. See the symmetry condition in [Arias-Castro, §18.1.2, Proposition 18.9](https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~eariasca/index_files/principles_of_statistical_analysis_free_v1.0.pdf). No stronger statistical claim follows from seed 7.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:60:| v4 RecipeDeleteMultipleRecipes | adb `whoami` SIGTRAP during database setup | 1081798181 | 11 / 0 |
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:63:| GUI-Owl SimpleSmsResend | gRPC-polluted adb time query in initialization | 3808889176 | 7 / 1 |
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:69:Across arms, the only goal mismatch is `MarkorCreateFolder`: the name contains each run's wall-clock timestamp ([generator](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/single/markor.py:162)). All arms fail it, so this imperfect pairing contributes zero to the observed difference. Nor does a matching Python seed guarantee byte-identical environments: the video generator uses [unseeded NumPy noise](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/utils/user_data_generation.py:246), and some database IDs use UUIDs. No differing task goal/seed was found among the counted successes. The [per-success review](success_review.md) covers all 34 successes, including the legitimate zero-target spirulina deletion and the correctly repeated GUI-Owl SMS.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:73:Original local times on November 18: GUI-Owl **01:35–09:30**, emulator 5556; v1 **01:30–06:32**, emulator 5558; v4 **13:22–18:07**, emulator 5558. Each original log has one run start/end and no checkpoint-resume/skipped-task marker; episode timestamps do not show a pause/restart. The preregistered possibility of pausing v1 is not evidence it actually occurred. Initial preregistration commit `29d5d25` predates the first launch, despite the approximate time in its heading.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:75:The first runner used by GUI-Owl/v1 differs from v4's later runner in logging/startup/exit handling. The resume/atomic-checkpoint changes do not give a saved seed-7 episode another attempt. Both primary arms receive the same app-list construction, one screenshot, temperature 0, one-second post-action waits and `int(10 × complexity)` steps. [Static budget and episode checks](execution_checks.json) find no over-budget episode across originals/retries. The actual per-episode app-list text was not persisted, so exact installed-package equality cannot be proved from the episodes.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:77:[Original runner](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/local_sealed_aw_v3.sh:26) and [retry runner](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/local_aw_rerun.sh:21) use the same per-arm model/mmproj paths and inference flags. v4 uses 774,400 input pixels, 1,024 image-token cap, context 8,192, output cap 512; GUI-Owl uses 1,048,576 pixels, cap 2,600, context 20,480, output cap 256. These are matched-input adaptations, not identical compute allocations. No recorded generation reaches either output cap (observed maxima 68/114), and no LFM parse retry occurs. The app list and v4 prompt are declared differences from the v1 reference, not a controlled model-only comparison.
results/codex/seed7_analysis_audit/report.md:79:Both November 19 retries run sequentially on emulator 5558, so GUI-Owl's retry changes device instance from 5556. The prescribed model/prompt/server configuration remains the same; the recorded evidence does not establish a systematic advantage from that move. Server logs corroborate model paths, but do not supply run-time weight hashes. No observed configuration change, capped-output asymmetry, unended success, or selective retry establishes a v4-favoring protocol violation. These limits, the checker error and subset correction are why the verdict is **VALID WITH CAVEATS**, with the result still **PRELIMINARY**.
34:The FA probe itself is verified: `fa_probe/requests_maiui_fa.jsonl:1` reports **1,176.146 s**, comprising **1,066.243 s prompt** and **107.955 s generation**, 3,035 prompt tokens and **2,048 output tokens**, `finish_reason="length"`, with repeated `<thinking>` output. `server_maiui_fa.log:4,6,54–56` confirms Q4_K_M, four threads and matching timings. Its memory samples show **VmSwap=0 throughout**. This is a completed HTTP call yielding an invalid action, and `bench_maiui_fa.json` labels it **rep 0/warm-up**, not a timed successful step. Phone-side timing rules out tunnel/curl/output buffering as the explanation for this call's 1,066-second prompt time. One probe does not isolate quantization or FA as the cause.
38:GUI-Owl's client logged timeout failures at 16:13:23, 16:19:25 and 16:25:28 (`client_guiowl.log:33–44`); the worker then stopped its server. That approximately 18-minute allowance is shorter than the successful FA probe's 19.6 minutes. MAI-UI also logged repeated timeouts (`client_maiui.log:38–39`). Retries can queue duplicates while earlier phone curls continue. Thus “no call completed before cancellation” is accurate; timeout-free, indefinitely stalled execution was not demonstrated. Curl's 1,800-second limit and the subprocess's 2,000-second limit (`record_proxy_adb.py:42–44`) are separate limits, not substitutes for client policy.
40:**P2 A5 — fsync protects completed records, not an inventory of requests.** `record_proxy_adb.py:60–77` writes only after `phone_http` returns. The worker terminates the proxy after the client exits (`devstream_device_v5.sh:99`); neither failed arm has a request JSONL despite server-side work. A stop mid-request therefore leaves no durable start, attempt identity or cancellation record. Threads append in completion order; `devstream_report.py:19–21` then drops the first *successful completion*, which cannot reliably identify warm-up after retries/failures. Add durable start/finish events with request/case/pass/warm-up/attempt IDs and preserve or drain in-flight work. No loss or mispairing was found in the 16 completed v4 records.
68:Recounting only the 105 named tasks, excluding six backup directories, yields **104 result files, five successes, 5/105 = 4.7619%**. Successes: TakeSelfieTask, OpenFlightModeTask, CloseFlightModeTask, AdjustFontIconMinimumTask, SendWaiverTask. ThanksgivingPrepTask remains an initialization HTTP-500 failure after four attempts (`Traj/ThanksgivingPrepTask/thread_135128759621312.log:5–20`; `v4_full.log:44793–44794`). All task score/presence fields match `v4_gui_en_summary.json`; elapsed time also matches **22,860 s**.
79:Given the reported 14:09 GUI-Owl OOM, invalidating `guiowl_gui_en` and starting a **fresh full** `guiowl_gui_en_r2` is correct; do not retain its four successes or stitch attempts. The raw Colab OOM/r2 startup logs were not available in the inspected local artifacts, so that incident and current remote flags remain user-supplied premises. The checked-in launcher still omits the reported recovery flag `--cache-ram 0` (`scripts/colab_mw_models.sh:17–22`); record the actual restart command/configuration for reproducibility.

