docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/architecture_hparams.md:5:Comparability warning used throughout: AW numbers below are mostly self-reported by model authors in their own harness (own prompt, own history format, often multiple history screenshots, sometimes pass@3). They are not directly comparable to our 1-screenshot harness. The clearest proof is our own measurement: GUI-Owl-1.5-2B scores 67.9 in its authors' report but 19.8% (23/116) in our 1-image harness.
docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/architecture_hparams.md:10:By late 2026 the best end-to-end <=4B agents report 50-70% on AW: GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (67.9), GUI-Owl-1.5-4B (69.8), Step-GUI-4B (63.9 pass@1), UI-Venus-1.5-2B (55.6), MIRAGE-4B (52.6) and MAI-UI-2B (49.1). The plain base Qwen3-VL-2B gets 36.4 and Qwen3-VL-4B gets 45.3. All of the leaders are built on Qwen3-VL and use multi-stage pipelines: large GUI mid-training or SFT (millions of samples, or 10B tokens), then offline and/or online RL in live emulators. All use their own harnesses, which usually include several history screenshots. The older 3B generation (Ferret-UI Lite 28.0, ScaleCUA-3B 23.7) sits near 25-30%. Our 12.9% is low next to the reported numbers, but it is in the same range as GUI-Owl-1.5-2B measured in our own harness (19.8%).
docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/architecture_hparams.md:14:- **GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct: 67.9 AW** (OSWorld-Verified 43.5, MobileWorld 31.3). **GUI-Owl-1.5-4B-Instruct: 69.8 AW**. 8B-Instruct: 69.0. 8B-Thinking: 71.6. 32B-Instruct: 69.8. — [Mobile-Agent-v3.5 / GUI-Owl-1.5 report, Table 1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16855); 67.9 also on the [HF model card](https://huggingface.co/mPLUG/GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct)
docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/architecture_hparams.md:48:- **Our harness costs GUI-Owl-1.5-2B about 48 points** (67.9 reported vs 19.8 measured). The likely causes are fewer history screenshots (1 vs up to 5), a different prompt or history format (they re-feed thoughts/conclusions), resolution, and max-step settings. Under our harness, LFM3-2B (12.9%) trails GUI-Owl-1.5-2B by ~7 points, not ~55.
docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/online_rl.md:47:  Table 1 lists GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct at 67.9 on AW and 31.3 on MobileWorld; 4B-Instruct 69.8; 8B-Instruct 69.0; 8B-Thinking 71.6. The 2B/4B values were extracted by a fetch tool from the HTML table, so re-verify. — [Mobile-Agent-v3.5, arXiv 2602.16855](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16855); [HTML Table 1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.16855v1)
docs/research/notes/small-gui-agent-training-methods/online_rl.md:119:| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct | SFT + MRPO (RL delta not reported) | AW 67.9 (paper's own harness) | [2602.16855](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.16855v1) |
docs/research/notes/beating-gui-owl-at-2b-fairly/gui_owl_recipe.md:311:- GUI-Owl is evidently trained to work with both 1-image + text-conclusion history (v1 harness, MobileWorld default) and a 5-image window (v3.5 AW harness). Which mode the 2B's 67.9 used is answered by the released AW code (5 images). Whether the paper run used exactly this code is not stated.
docs/research/notes/beating-gui-owl-at-2b-fairly/gui_owl_recipe.md:323:- GUI-Owl-1.5 end-to-end: 2B-Instruct 67.9, 4B-Instruct 69.8, 8B-Instruct 69.0, 8B-Thinking 71.6, 32B-Instruct 69.8, 32B-Thinking 69.8. The HF card shows 69.4 and 68.2 for the two 32B models.
docs/research/notes/beating-gui-owl-at-2b-fairly/gui_owl_recipe.md:333:| 2B-Instruct | 43.5 | **67.9** | 33.0 | 31.3 | 25.78 |
docs/research/notes/beating-gui-owl-at-2b-fairly/gui_owl_recipe.md:393:- The family's AW numbers are almost flat across sizes (67.9 to 71.6). Either AW is near a ceiling for this recipe, or AW-like data dominates (inferred).
