+## E. Human readability and unnecessary tree content
+
+Most new pages successfully use short introductions, tables and bullets. The following specific rewrites would finish that job without hiding limitations:
+
+| Location | Concrete rewrite |
+|---|---|
+| `docs/repository.md:45`–`:51` | Main table: `Analysis — 11 scripts — analysis/`; `AndroidWorld — 18 scripts — scripts/androidworld/`; `Training — 32 scripts + 30 jobs — scripts/training/`. Follow with a linked one-file-per-row move manifest. Keep the removal reasons separate and fix the handoff exception. |
+| `docs/history-rewrites.md:73` | Subject: **“Seed-7 audit fixes: template subset, CI and checker dispute.”** Put the full historical commit subject in a collapsible detail or link to the commit. The hash mapping remains unchanged. |
+| `docs/evaluation.md:13` | Split into rows for benchmark, screenshots, pixel ceiling, token ceiling, quantisation, app list and parse retries; use separate AndroidWorld and MobileWorld tables. This also prevents the misleading “same” claims from spanning different experiments. |
+| `docs/evaluation.md:144`, `docs/evaluation.md:146` | Short table cells: **“CPU: 5 cases; 14/4/4 retained calls after cache exclusions.”** **“Phone: 4 CPU threads; two evaluation-ceiling competitor calls; two 5-case equal-ceiling passes.”** Put hardware, SHA checks and launcher links in short bullets immediately below. |
